%N A399477 a(n) = 9*binomial(n,8) + 49*binomial(n,7) + 75*binomial(n,6) + 35*binomial(n,5) + 3*binomial(n,4).
%C A399477 Place n points in general position on a circle, join them in all possible ways; how many (non- and self-intersecting) quadrilaterals can be seen?
%D A399477 G. Tollisen and T. Lengyel, A finite difference approach to counting quadrangles in a circle, Geombinatorics, 20 (2011), 168-179.
%H A399477 Lucas R. Scatalani, <a href="/A399477/b399477.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 4..10000</a>
%H A399477 <a href="/index/Rec#order_09">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (9,-36,84,-126,126,-84,36,-9,1).
%F A399477 a(n) = 9*binomial(n,8) + 49*binomial(n,7) + 75*binomial(n,6) + 35*binomial(n,5) + 3*binomial(n,4).
%F A399477 From _Jianing Song_, Aug 30 2026: (Start)
%F A399477 a(n) = n*(n - 1)*(n - 2)*(n - 3)*(9*n^4 + 194*n^3 - 69*n^2 - 2774*n + 2520)/40320.
%F A399477 G.f.: x^4*(3 + 23*x - 12*x^2 - 8*x^3 + 3*x^4)/(1 - x)^9.
%F A399477 E.g.f.: x^4*(5040 + 11760*x + 4200*x^2 + 392*x^3 + 9*x^4)*exp(x)/40320. (End)
